# Case of the Gorgon's Kiss: "When this Case enters, destroy up to one target creature that was dealt damage this turn." (CR 115.1, 701.8a, 603.3d) On turn 3 Bot1's two Memnites attack and Bot2 blocks each with an Ornithopter,
# each of which is dealt 1 damage (and survives, 0/2). After combat Bot1 casts the Case: Bot2's undamaged Memnite and Bot1's own Memnites (dealt no damage, the Ornithopters have 0 power) may not be chosen, a damaged
# Ornithopter may, "up to one" refuses naming both damaged Ornithopters, and the one chosen is destroyed while the other stays.

[Bot1 Deck]
Memnite
Memnite
Mox Jet
Case of the Gorgon's Kiss
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Memnite
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Mountain x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Memnite#1 > Bot2; Memnite#2 > Bot2)
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter#1 > Memnite#1; Ornithopter#2 > Memnite#2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1.Damage = 1
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2.Damage = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Case of the Gorgon's Kiss.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Memnite)
! Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite#1)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1; Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield = Memnite; Ornithopter
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield = Case of the Gorgon's Kiss; Memnite; Memnite; Mox Jet
